      "seed": 91970201,
      "version": 90,
      "versionNonce": 2029173079,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787081449196,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "OpenTelemetry\nThe Industry Standard\nBefore OpenTelemetry, every observability vendor\nhad proprietary SDKs and formats. If you wanted\nto switch from Jaeger to Zipkin, you'd re-\ninstrument your entire codebase. This vendor lock-\nin meant architectural decisions became permanent\ncommitments.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Njf8mRqXDxullppY97Jpb",
      "originalText": "OpenTelemetry\nThe Industry Standard\nBefore OpenTelemetry, every observability vendor had proprietary SDKs and formats. If you wanted to switch from Jaeger to Zipkin, you'd re-instrument your entire codebase. This vendor lock-in meant architectural decisions became permanent commitments.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
